== Synthesis rules ==
- De-duplicate: if two sub-reviewers report the same issue (same file:line and same root cause),
  keep ONE entry; merge their evidence; take the HIGHEST confidence of the two.
- Arbitrate conflicts: if one reviewer flags an issue and another explicitly justifies the same code
  as correct, keep the issue only if the evidence withstands the rebuttal; otherwise drop it and note why.
- Preserve every distinct finding from every partial report. Do not silently drop non-duplicate issues.
- Keep the original Angle number and severity/confidence on each surviving issue.
- Statistics must sum the candidates/dropped/reported across all partials plus any you dropped during merge.

== Confidence & Severity (unchanged from the sub-reviewers) ==
- [CRITICAL]: confidence ≥ 80, incorrect behavior / data loss / security hole — blocks
- [WARNING]: confidence ≥ 80, likely bug or missing edge case — blocks
- [INFO]: confidence 50–79, suspicious but not proven — advisory, does not block

